{"p4": {"friction": "Restated results such as \"Theorem 1.1 (Corollary 5.2)\" have no relation type that fits cleanly. equivalent-to needs an asserted identity, and the two statements differ in part (2) (affine vs FSch^qt). Also, \"this construction defines a contravariant functor Spec\" (Prop. 4.7) uses the word 'defines' inside a proved result.", "doubt": "Claim 6: how to type an introduction restatement. Claim 5: defines vs proves when a proposition gives functor structure to an already-defined object. Claim 15: whether leaving out the theorem's standing hypotheses makes a claim unfaithful.", "missing_context": "The paper's proofs and Section 5–6 prose, which are not in the input (it is statements only). There was no text showing how Theorem 1.1 relates to Corollary 5.2 beyond the parenthetical.", "proposed_change": "Add a rubric rule for restated results ('Theorem X (Corollary Y)'): either type them equivalent-to with a new sense 'restatement', or exclude them from extraction. Also state whether a claim that omits a result's hypotheses counts as faithful.", "process_observation": "Several claims are near-duplicates (2 and 10; 9 and 18), which inflates the faithful count. Two proves claims have object subjects (1, 4), a recurring extractor pattern."}}
